        "(b) The original strand contains 4 A/T bases (A, T, A, and the T pairing with the first A) and 3 G/C bases (C, C, G) &mdash; more precisely: A&ndash;T pairs occur at positions 1, 2, 6, 7 (4 pairs, 2 H-bonds each = 8 H-bonds) and G&ndash;C pairs occur at positions 3, 4, 5 (3 pairs, 3 H-bonds each = 9 H-bonds), giving a total of 8 + 9 = 17 hydrogen bonds across this 7-base-pair section."
